::kind(writ)

=[ Writ: workspace root ]

Rules the sisho-board repository obeys.

Only the author edits this file. An agent that finds a rule in its way
proposes an edit here and stops. It does not work around the rule, and it
does not relax the rule to fit the change it wanted to make.

==[ crate-layering ]

@rule(crate-layering){
  guard: (twrit: layers)

  layers: (
    3: ("app")
    2: ("crates/sisho-board-tui")
    1: ("crates/sisho-board-core", "crates/sisho-board-health")
    0: ("crates/sisho-board-run", "crates/sisho-board-sdk")
  )
}

Every workspace member belongs to exactly one layer, and depends only on
layers strictly below its own. Same-layer dependencies are allowed;
upward ones are not.

Layer 0 holds the Board Pane disclosure protocol SDK (`sisho-board-sdk`) and
the jobserver-gated subprocess runner (`sisho-board-run`).
Layer 1 holds the pure state machine and trust delegation (`sisho-board-core`)
and the Vault Readiness & Health / link-check engine (`sisho-board-health`).
Layer 2 holds the Ratatui terminal UI and interactive event loop (`sisho-board-tui`).
Layer 3 is the CLI program (`app`).

==[ process-door ]

@rule(process-door){
  guard: (twrit: door)

  door: (
    names:   ("std::process")
    within:  ("crates/*")
    allowed: ("crates/sisho-board-run")
  )
}

Only `crates/sisho-board-run` spawns or inspects subprocesses via `std::process`
inside `crates/*`, ensuring all subprocess execution goes through the
jobserver-gated runner.

==[ no-tui-in-core ]

@rule(no-tui-in-core){
  guard: (twrit: door)

  door: (
    names:   ("ratatui", "crossterm")
    within:  ("crates/*")
    allowed: ("crates/sisho-board-tui")
  )
}

Only `crates/sisho-board-tui` depends on or imports `ratatui` or `crossterm`
inside `crates/*`, keeping Layer 0 and Layer 1 crates TUI-free.

==[ no-sisho-crates ]

@rule(no-sisho-crates){
  guard: (twrit: door)

  door: (
    names:   ("sisho_run", "sisho_tools", "sisho_vault", "sisho_serve", "sisho_tui", "sisho_cli")
    allowed: ()
  )
}

`sisho-board` depends on no internal `sisho-*` crate (only `sisho-sdk` for the
extension protocol). The extension knows the contract, not the orchestrator's
internals.

==[ tmtroot-output-not-edited ]

@rule(tmtroot-output-not-edited){
  guard: (runs: "just docs-check")
}

A file exported from @dir(tmtroot/) is generated. Do not hand-edit it. Edit
the source and re-export.

==[ rust-api-docs ]

@rule(rust-api-docs){
  guard: (twrit: rust-api)

  rust_api: (
    out: "tmtroot/generated/crates"
  )
}

API documentation for all workspace Rust crates must be kept up to date
with the source code and inner doc-comments (`//!`, `///`).
